  "narrative": "Marisol Trading, an Amsterdam marketplace seller, runs a sourcing agent under a $500 per-order cap. On 2026-08-18 it built a $2,182.00 order from Globalsource — more than four times the cap. The firm's own blocking control MAR-CTL-002 evaluated the order and triggered correctly, and an operations analyst overrode it thirty-one seconds later with the reason 'seasonal pre-buy, approved verbally by category lead'. Two findings, on two different axes: the cap breach itself, and the fact that the control designed to stop it worked and a person switched it off. The second is the more serious supervisory fact — it is a conduct question, not a technical failure, and the override log names who. The merchant is a marketplace and its sub-merchant is properly disclosed, so counterparty fronting is NOT in play here.",
